A||||10||jelly2m8||7" rims on front of an 88?||||1||
Z||000000||jelly2m8||10-13-2001||11:07 PM||||Anybody use the 15x7" wheels on front of an 88?<P> Going to be putting a 88 chassis under my 87.<BR> Just wondering if their are any draw backs performance wise in using these rims on the front.<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||LT1 Chop Top||10-13-2001||11:24 PM||||I have 16x7.5 in the front of my 88.  Tires are 235-45-16.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-13-2001||11:57 PM||||ChopTop...I asked you before about offset and you said you didn't know what it was.  Could you please check the offset if you have the wheels off anytime?  It's pretty easy to measure, just need measurements of the overall wheel width and the distance from the backside of the wheel to the bolt-up area.  I dunno if you'll ever have the wheels off the front...but that'd be AWESOME if you checked that.  Thanks <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||sloth85GT||10-14-2001||12:06 AM||||I don't know if an 85 is too different from an 88 regarding this topic, but I have 15x7's with a 35mm offset on my car. 35mm is the lowest I could go though. Don't know if that helps or not. <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jncomutt||10-14-2001||12:32 AM||||7 inch rims??  I think my scooter has bigger wheels... hehe... (sarcasm intended)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||10-14-2001||12:07 PM||||Yes, 88s are different in this regard.  This has been covered lots, with pics, if you want to do a search.  Short answer, yes you can put the factory 15x7 rims on the front of an 88, but they will stick out of the fender about a half inch or so.  I think it makes it look funny.  The 88's have a wider front suspension, and that's why they went to the different rims on the front of the 88's.  BTW, the 88 coupes use the same 14" rims all the way around, and yes, the fronts on those stick out some too, but it's not as noticeable on a smaller rim.<P>If you're going with aftermarket rims, get whatever you want.  I'd recommend 40-45mm offset (42mm or so) for a 7" wide rim.||||reg||6
Z||000006||jelly2m8||10-14-2001||02:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>Yes, Short answer, yes you can put the factory 15x7 rims on the front of an 88, but they will stick out of the fender about a half inch or so.  I think it makes it look funny.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Sounds good to me. I have the Grand Am brakes on front of the 87 car now, and the wheels stick out about a half an inch or so. I am used to the way it looks, and satisfied with it.<P>Thanks for the info!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula||10-14-2001||02:51 PM||||I have 15x7s on the front of my formula and the only thing I dont like is the wheel gap, but thats a height problem.||||reg||1
