Z||000009||jelly2m8||10-14-2001||11:32 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jimmybpei:<BR><B>jelly, <BR> <BR>I was wondering if my wheeles stuck out a bit since the brake upgrade, and i guess they so. Why didn't you put the grand am brakes in the back too, i did. but haven't driven the car enough in the last year to tell the diff. (onnly 5kms since the upgrade)<P>Oh yeah the module that rockcrawl sent me was mailed on the 11th so hoping by friday it will be running.<P>Do you know of any fastback clips for sale, <BR>complete. GTBOY has one for sale in barrie, ont that i may pick up in 2 weeks if he still has it.<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Jimmy.<BR> I left the stock brakes on the fastback, because I wanted the park brake on it. plus its mandatory here in N.S.<P> The V8 on the other hand has the GA's all the way around, boy that does make a difference.<P> looking forward getting your way soon to check out your projects.<BR> I am (hopefully)heading to Maine next week to pick up a 88 chassis. lmk if you need any parts, this guy seems to have a few things, and his prices seem fair.<BR> dude, I need yer phone number, I'd like ta give u a call sometime.<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||qwikgta||10-15-2001||10:53 PM||||Im running 16x7 Beretta GTZ rims on my 88 with 205/50 up front and 225/50 out back.  I think the offset is diff from the Fiero rims becasue I was running the stock Crosslace rims off my 87 GT on it and the front did stick out more than I wanted.  The first thing I noticed with the GTZ rims is that the front did not stick out as much.  I know the offset is diff because I was not sure they would fit my 88 so I checked them before I bought them and I noticed that I could just get the tip of my finger between the brake and the rim on the GTZ rims and I could get a lot more with the Crosslace rims. Felt like about a half an inch diff in offset, in a good way.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 66K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, GT rear swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails, KYB's, dropped springs.<P>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject/robsfieroproject.html<BR>   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
